From 2ac6dc79086fb74445d644a2f4200aabd7728168 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen35 <qwen35@local>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:09:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [GPU] Work-group cooperative scaled-state
 PagedGatedDeltaNet prefill kernel

The gated-delta-rule recurrence in paged_gated_delta_net_opt is instruction-issue bound
(XVE 77% active, ~315 instructions per thread and token, ~12 GB/s of DRAM traffic): every
sub-group redundantly loads/L2-normalises q and k and computes exp(gate) and beta for each
token, and the decay multiplies the whole state every token.

For multi-token prefill (Xe2/Xe3, sub-group 16, K head dim 128, float8 vectors) a new
fast path is used:

* one work-group per (sequence, value head) with V_HEAD_DIM / 8 sub-groups, each owning 8
  rows of the [V_HEAD_DIM x K_HEAD_DIM] state;
* the state-independent per-token work (q/k load and L2 norm, q.k, exp(gate), beta) is done
  once per work-group, GDN_CHUNK = 4 tokens at a time by different sub-groups, and handed to
  the others through a double-buffered SLM tile;
* the state is kept as S_true = c * S with a scalar c, so the decay only updates c, and
  the delta rule is rearranged so that both dot products use the old state
  (a = S.k, b = S.q, u = (v - c'a) * beta, S += (u / c') k, out = c' b + u (k.q));
  S is renormalised when c' leaves [1e-6, 1e6] and before it is written back.

Decode (1 token) and shapes that do not fit keep the original kernel.

Unit tests: seven new paged_gated_delta_net cases (long sequences, several chunks, tails
that are not a multiple of the chunk, f16/f32). The f16 cases use gate <= 0 because gate in
[-1, 1] makes the state grow and fails the original kernel too.
